{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvatuP1K1uD2TgprK3vM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`contract/claim.compact` is written and compiles cleanly with compiler 0.36.0. I only ran the fast compile, so no proving keys were generated, and I haven't run the contract.\n\n- **Names and types:** the contract has the witness `secretKey(): Bytes<32>`, the exported pure circuit `publicKey(sk)` and the exported circuit `claim(): []`. There are no other witnesses.\n- **Claim:** `claim()` derives a nullifier from the secret key and fails with \"Already claimed\" if that nullifier is already in the ledger set. Otherwise it records the nullifier and increments the public counter `claims`.\n- **Privacy:** the public key is a hash of the secret key with the prefix `claim:pk:`. The nullifier is a hash of the same secret key with a different prefix, `claim:nullifier:`. Someone who sees a public key can't compute the matching nullifier without the secret key. So the ledger doesn't show whether a given public key has claimed.\n\nThe ledger does reveal how many claims have happened, because that count is public by design."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":733,"cache_read_input_tokens":21437,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":733},"output_tokens":352,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6d83e83-5a10-4400-84a1-5f76aebaf078","uuid":"d9b26697-8a90-47a2-aedf-62ad7046843a","timestamp":"2026-11-11T05:25:54.735Z","request_id":"req_011Cgvatu87zR1UUy3tkdREv"}
